{{also|drücken}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*þrukjaną||to press}}, {{m|gem-pro|*þrūganą||to threaten}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*trūk-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*trūg-||to press, beat}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|drukken||to press, print|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|trykke||to press|lang=da}}, {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|thrutch||to throng|lang=en}} and, outside Germanic, with {{etyl|sq|-}} {{term|ndryqem||to stretch|lang=sq}}. Closely cognate with {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|drücken||to press, push|lang=de}}: ''drucken'' is originally the southern form; the first German printers were in the south.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈdʁʊkŋ̩]|[ˈdʁʊkən]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-drucken.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-drucken.ogg|Audio (Austria)|lang=de}}

